;; Arc 251.8d-ii (EIGHTH DRAW) — WALL row 2 (NEGATIVE, must fail startup).
;;
;; THE DIRECTION CONTROL. A KEYWORD author writing the OTHER join against a correctly
;; stored `/` name must stay REFUSED — 255.8's WEIGH ruled that the wrong-join
;; acceptance is the thing to close, not to spread. The cure flips `/` -> `::` only,
;; never `::` -> `/`.
;;
;; ⛔ The parent is LOWER-CASE on purpose. Written with a PascalCase parent this row
;; would spell `:user::Box::of` — the colon-joined Type::member that 255.4 RETIRED, and
;; `tests/lint/one_member_join.rs` refuses that text in any tracked `.wat`, `.wat.bad`
;; included. (It caught the first draft of this file, which is its own corroboration:
;; the direction this stone declines to implement is already corpus-illegal.) A
;; lower-case parent tests the same direction without writing a retired spelling.
(:wat::core::defmacro :user::helper/of [n <- :wat::WatAST] -> :wat::WatAST
  `(:wat::core::+ ~n 1))
(:wat::core::defn :user::entry [] -> :wat::core::i64
  (:user::helper::of 7))
